4. Backend Development
The backend manages application logic and communication between the frontend, database, and Gemini.

Example API structure
POST /api/auth/register
POST /api/auth/login

GET  /api/profile
PUT  /api/profile

POST /api/plans/generate
GET  /api/plans

GET  /api/workouts/today
POST /api/workouts/:id/complete

POST /api/exercises/:id/replace

GET  /api/progress
The backend should validate requests before sending information to Gemini.

