11. Error Handling
The application should handle situations such as:

Gemini API unavailable

Invalid user input

Invalid AI-generated JSON

Database connection failure

Authentication failure

Network timeout

Example:

Gemini Request
     ↓
Response?
 ┌───┴────┐
Yes       No
 ↓         ↓
Validate   Error Handler
 ↓         ↓
Save       Retry/Fallback
The application should never assume that an AI response is automatically valid.

12. Security During Development
Important practices include:

Store Gemini credentials in environment variables.

Never expose API keys in frontend code.

Validate all user input.

Authenticate API requests.

Restrict users to their own data.

Secure database access.

Avoid storing unnecessary sensitive information.

